# Use Serena for coding work

Before any coding task in this repo:
1. Call MCP `initial_instructions` once per session via `CallMcpTool`.
2. Prefer Serena symbol tools over raw Grep/Read for PHP class/method navigation and edits.
3. Skip Serena only for: pure questions with no file changes, git/PR-only work, docs/CI-only changes, or browser verification (use IronBee instead).

Subagents spawned for coding must follow the same rules.

## MCP server identifier (critical)

`.cursor/mcp.json` registers the server as `serena`, but **`CallMcpTool` must use the runtime server id**:

`project-0-1.2.6-serena`

Using `server: "serena"` fails with `Tool serena-<tool> not found`.

Example:

```json
{
  "server": "project-0-1.2.6-serena",
  "toolName": "find_symbol",
  "arguments": {
    "name_path_pattern": "UPSDotCom/install",
    "relative_path": "upsdotcom/upsdotcom.php",
    "include_body": true,
    "max_matches": 1
  }
}
```

Tool schemas live under the MCP descriptors folder for `project-0-1.2.6-serena` (see Cursor MCP file system). There is no `tool_search` tool in this Cursor integration — read schemas from those JSON files or call tools directly.

## When to use Serena vs built-in tools

| Task | Tool |
|------|------|
| List symbols in a PHP file | `get_symbols_overview` |
| Find class/method/function by name | `find_symbol` (use function name, not filename) |
| Find callers | `find_referencing_symbols` |
| Replace a whole method/class | `replace_symbol_body` |
| Small in-method edit | `replace_content` |
| Non-PHP files, configs, markdown, tickets | Built-in Read/Grep/Edit |
| Text search across repo (discovery) | Grep, then Serena for symbol bodies |

Serena line numbers are **0-based**. Class names in this module are often `UPSDotCom` (capital UPS), not `UpsDotCom`.